# TIP4P/2005 water and Joung-Cheatham 2008 ions (TIP4P-Ew set).
# TIP4P/2005 has no ion parameters in that paper. The TIP4P-Ew
# Na+ and Cl- values are the Joung-Cheatham set used with it.
# Lorentz-Berthelot mixing is pair_modify mix arithmetic.
# sigma = Rmin/2 * 2^(5/6), epsilon in kcal/mol, lengths in angstrom.
#
#   Na+  Rmin/2 = 1.226  epsilon = 0.1684375  sigma = 2.184479
#   Cl-  Rmin/2 = 2.760  epsilon = 0.0116615  sigma = 4.917814
#
# Water: epsilon_O = 0.1852, sigma_O = 3.1589, q_H = 0.5564,
# q_M = -1.1128 on the oxygen (the pair style places the M site),
# d_OM = 0.1546, r_OH = 0.9572, angle = 104.52.
#
# regenerate.py writes the data file and sets datafile and nsteps.
# For an ice slab it inserts a freeze of molecule ids 1 through the
# ice count in place of the velocity line below.

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

variable datafile index data.brine
variable nsteps index 0
variable temp index 270

read_data ${datafile}

pair_style lj/cut/tip4p/long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 10.0
pair_modify mix arithmetic
kspace_style pppm/tip4p 1.0e-4
pair_coeff 1 1 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff 2 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff 3 3 0.1684375 2.184479
pair_coeff 4 4 0.0116615 4.917814

bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff 1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style harmonic
angle_coeff 1 55.0 104.52
special_bonds lj/coul 0.0 0.0 0.0

neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes
timestep 1.0
thermo 50

velocity all create ${temp} 12345 dist gaussian

fix rigid all shake 0.0001 20 0 b 1 a 1
minimize 1.0e-4 1.0e-6 20 200
run ${nsteps}
write_dump all custom dump.lammpstrj id mol type x y z
